      "text": "- Desktop secrets use Electron `safeStorage`; never put API keys in environment variables or plaintext config. The hosted exception below is explicit. Optional cloud integrations require a current plan, service boundary, redaction, focused tests, and applicable manifest changes, and must fail closed or degrade without breaking local chat. Never read, copy, or expose another tool's credentials (for example the Codex CLI's `~/.codex/auth.json`); the `codex-cli` engine lets the CLI use its own login. The ChatGPT sign-in runs Jenny's own OAuth flow, keeps its tokens only in the safeStorage-backed secure store, sends the access token only to the sidecar and the ChatGPT backend, and never shows tokens in the renderer or logs. Do not integrate Anthropic subscription auth.",
      "sha256": "4262f03c7ebb047e6d073ffcb1feb8f2370abcf8ef163d8da76799b298cdf296"
    }
  ],
  "Q05": [
    {
      "path": "AGENTS.md",
      "locator": "L37-37",
      "text": "- `tool.request_approval` blocks until an explicit approve/deny response. Other documented reverse requests are `tool.execute_electron` and versioned internal `runtime.operation` admission. The latter is not a model tool; `workspace_test.*` methods are the private contained-helper protocol. Filesystem tools require explicitly bound session/project authority; a null root permits conversation only.",
      "sha256": "4262f03c7ebb047e6d073ffcb1feb8f2370abcf8ef163d8da76799b298cdf296"
    }
  ],
